A method for determining separation strength of a joint between a first generally cup-shaped or cylindrical member and a second generally cup-shaped or cylindrical member, the method comprising:

securing an exterior sidewall surface of the first member with a clamping fixture;

engaging and supporting an annular rim defining an open end of the second member with a support fixture;

suspending the first and second members as an assembled structure by the support fixture; and

applying a tensile pulling force to the first member relative to the second member until the joint between the first member and the second member separates, thereby determining a separation strength of the joint based on the applied pulling force at separation.

A method for measuring bonding strength, comprising the steps of:

preparing a first measurement member and a second measurement member, each of the first and second measurement members having a cylindrical shape or a cup shape and having an opening;

joining the first measurement member and the second measurement member to each other at their respective openings;

fixing the first measurement member to a fixing member;

holding the second measurement member in a suspended state in midair; and

applying a tensile force in a direction separating the second measurement member from the first measurement member, thereby pulling the first measurement member and the second measurement member apart from each other.
